messages:
jordan (ACME): Hi, after switching to your OpenAI-compatible endpoint, our function calls started failing in production. Getting schema validation errors from our server.

support-bot: Thanks for reporting — I've created a ticket and forwarded logs to the support queue. Can you share a minimal repro? :wave:

jordan (ACME): repro below. We send a function definition with an enum for `status` (values: \"ACTIVE\", \"INACTIVE\") and the model returns a function_call where arguments are a JSON string with numeric codes (\"1\") instead of enum strings. Sample response pasted.

mina: can you paste the raw response body (not the parsed object)? need to see whether the arguments field is a string or object.

jordan (ACME): raw response snippet: ```json
{
  "id":"resp-01",
  "choices":[{
    "message":{
      "role":"assistant",
      "content":null,
      "function_call":{
        "name":"update_user",
        "arguments":"{\"user_id\":\"123\",\"status\":\"1\"}"
      }
    }
  }]
}
```

samir: ok, that shows `function_call.arguments` is a string (double-encoded). OpenAI spec allows that in some SDKs (arg string), but our backend's function deserializer expects an object and then validates enum values. the \"1\" is the enum code (legacy) so validation fails. Which client are you using to call Redwood?

jordan (ACME): server-side we call the Redwood endpoint directly via curl from our backend. example request: ```bash
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.example/v1/chat/completions \\  -H 'Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN' \\  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\  -d '{
    "model":"acme-compat-1",
    "messages":[{"role":"user","content":"update user 123 to active"}],
    "functions":[{
      "name":"update_user",
      "parameters":{
        "type":"object",
        "properties":{
          "user_id":{"type":"string"},
          "status":{"type":"string","enum":["ACTIVE","INACTIVE"]}
        },
        "required":["user_id","status"]
      }
    }]
  }'
```

mina: thanks. two things to check: 1) whether the model/service variant you're routing to is returning `arguments` as string (we've seen some older compatibility stacks do this), 2) whether your validator accepts stringified JSON and maps legacy numeric codes to enum names. we should not break by default.

samir: can you try POSTing the exact response payload to a small script that does JSON.parse on arguments, and show validation error? otherwise i can reproduce locally.

jordan (ACME): error we see in our app: `FunctionCallValidationError: status value \"1\" not in enum [ACTIVE, INACTIVE]` — stack trace pinned. We worked around by pre-processing the arguments string: `args = typeof args === 'string' ? JSON.parse(args) : args; args.status = map_code(args.status)` but that's brittle.

mina: agreed. this looks like a compatibility mismatch between OpenAI-style stringified `arguments` and our platform's expectation to provide enums as textual values. We'll escalate.

samir: quick repro I ran locally against the same model alias returns the same: `function_call.arguments` string with numeric codes. I suspect the model roll we use for that alias is an OpenAI shim that normalizes enum tokens to codes in some modes. filing an internal ticket.

ops-jen: created internal ops ticket INF-3247 and linked customer logs. Also added a short reproduction script and test case to the eng-ml queue. tagging @eng-ml for triage.

mina: next steps: (1) eng-ml to confirm whether model variant/compat shim is the source; (2) runtime team to allow automatic JSON.parse() of `function_call.arguments` before schema validation; (3) add a mapping layer for numeric enum codes -> canonical strings as a temporary mitigation.

samir: for mitigation, we can add a toggle in the console: \"lenient function_call parsing\" default off, enable per-customer. That buys time without risking global behavior changes.

jordan (ACME): appreciated. ETA on mitigation? our production traffic is impacted (several failing calls / minute).

ops-jen: short-term: i can enable a lenient parsing flag for your account and run a health check. will coordinate with devops.

mina: thx. jordan — can you DM me a request id from one failed call (x-request-id header) so we can correlate logs?

jordan (ACME): sent DM with id `req-2025-07-11-8421`.

support-bot: Update: lenient parsing enabled for ACME account. Please verify.

jordan (ACME): quick check looks good, function calls now accepted. thanks! :tada:

ops-jen: leaving this open until eng-ml completes root cause. assigned to samir for follow-up.

samir: i'll add a regression test to ensure we accept both stringified and object `arguments` and normalize legacy enum codes.

mina: moving to eng triage. will post final postmortem once root cause and release are done.

jordan (ACME): will monitor for a day and report back. cheers.
